readme=f"# Caller documentation ownership and template binders\n\nSource `{source}` extends the optional `inlineCompiler` classic-body action.\nAttached caller JSDoc follows the original lexical declaration after inserted\nstatements. The native source parser independently derives the widened edit\nextent; no provider range override exists. Exact comments/trivia move once in\nthe same lexical scope, retaining typedef identity and export ownership. Every removed\ndefinition leaves a fixed empty statement so a formerly trailing annotation cannot\nbecome leading documentation for generated storage. Trailing\ncomments that were not attached remain in place. No arbitrary printed type or\nanalyzed source execution is added. Existing bindings/types and application gates\nremain mandatory.\n\nWhen callee comments also declare module types, their copied function tags form\none contract comment. Keeping template, parameter and return tags together retains\ntheir common binder on inert source-function expressions. Original module type\ndeclarations remain at their original site. Original source pieces, not printed\ncompiler types, supply the contract. The raw worker observations are unchanged.\n\n| Frozen scope | Actual result |\n| --- | --- |\n| guard-r2, 811 unchanged native inputs | Sixteen body units; 117 integration passes / zero failures / two existing ignored across eight targets |\n| Format/build/all-target Clippy with warnings denied | Passed |\n| retained-r2, 805 unchanged inputs | Python 17, typecheck, TypeScript 260 passed / three existing skips |\n| Metadata after final checks | Python 17; all 811 native and 804 other retained inputs exact; only three R1 fields changed |\n\nOne new native integration function covers thirteen positive cases: the original\ncaller @type{{3}}/generic-factory regression, primitive annotations, exports,\ncombined/separate typedef comments, nested typedef shadows, interleaved comments,\nUnicode/CRLF/BOM, trailing unattached comments, multiple call sites and TS comments.\nTwo new units check native attachment/deadline/comment/whitespace bounds and actual\ncompiler effects with forged extents, type text, unknown fields and coherent output\nhashes. Seventeen CLI scenarios include two new strict JS regressions passing\nindependent tsc, verification, approval, application and foreign-preserving recovery.\nThe standalone current CLI admits the original regression, leaves source bytes\nunchanged and matches the final executable hash. Counts overlap; no addition.\n\nThe ownership-only prototype passes the original two counterprobes. The first\nactual-source worker run has eleven passes and one nested typedef failure:\nseparate copied comments lose the template binder, causing TS7006/TS2322. Its\nfull failing projection is retained in a diagnostic-only probe. After keeping\nfunction tags together, the twelve worker cases pass exact reported result types\nand owned runtime comparisons. Two further collector/typedef probes retain empty\nanonymous argument names and contextual callbacks. These worker requests have\nsynthetic snapshot IDs and claim no native admission. A further same-line trailing\ncomment fails after definition removal; an empty-statement prototype fixes it.\nThe final source always retains this boundary; all thirteen final worker cases pass. The native tests supply\nseparate real snapshot/source/binding/type/plan admission. Runtime oracles execute\nowned literal fixtures only; preparation executes no analyzed repository source.\n\nPrimary materialization checks {len(material)} paths: {materialization['raw']} raw\nand {materialization['utf8CrlfOnly']} UTF-8 CRLF-only matches. The protected PostgreSQL\nfixture is 2779 bytes and byte exact in both checkouts. No primary runtime rerun,\nwhole-native/Windows/current-head hosted/upstream certification, main merge or\nrelease is claimed. Actual TS generic frames, broader expected-result/predicate/\nparameter/annotation/diagnostic contexts, wider invocation/expression/declaration/\nlanguage/consumer semantics and other STATUS/R1-R9 requirements remain open.\n\nThe [index](index.json) binds {len(files)} raw artifacts with original probes,\nfailed projections, available runners/workers, source snapshots, regression logs,\nmetadata proofs, tool hashes and source materialization. Earlier archives remain\nimmutable.\n"
